The tests in this directory cover component behavior and numerical
migration contracts.

Install the package in an isolated environment, then run all tests from
the repository root:

$ uv sync --locked --extra torch-cpu --extra hdf5
$ uv run --no-sync python -m pytest -v

The CPU extra is the normal complete-suite selection. CUDA and two-GPU
evidence requires a trusted runner with the required resources and is not
silently replaced by a skipped local test. HDF5 tests remain optional when
PyTables is unavailable.

Write new tests as pytest-native functions or plain `Test*` classes with
direct assertions. Use `pytest.mark.parametrize` with stable semantic IDs for
independent cases; retain intentional stateful sequences. Focused fixtures and
finalizers must clean up patches, temporary resources, and runtime state after
failures. Future Taflove reproduction tests follow the same rules and must
state device, dtype, thread, and compile-policy requirements.

## Pytest migration map

[`pytest-migration-map.json`](pytest-migration-map.json) records the issue
#179 migration from the pinned unittest baseline. Each old method maps to a
current pytest node pattern and collection count; each former `subTest` is
classified without storing every collected node instance.

| Mapping kind | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `parametrized` | Independent old cases became pytest parameter cases; the pattern count records their collected nodes. |
| `retained-sequential` | The cases deliberately remain in one test; the entry carries an audited source-backed reason such as shared evolving state, artifact lifetime, cross-case comparison, failure aggregation, or ordered control. |

The validation test keeps the baseline counts, mappings, uniqueness, and zero
gap policy current when migrations change.
